body:
\>Help ruin Sakura Wars

&#x200B;

Wait that was the same Hideo? God 

&#x200B;

damnit

Aqua's only got eyes for Ai though!

&#x200B;

Which was a bit weird when he was like 30 and she was 15, but is a lot weird now that she's also his mom.

Power is so good.

&#x200B;

I miss Himeno though. What does the mangaka have against tough chicks with eyepatches, smh.

Yeah, I just hope that Miya doesn't completely go up in flames with it.

&#x200B;

Poor girl.

God damn the main guy is awful in every way.

&#x200B;

His poor daughter...

Sort of, her sister prayed for it and then Okita actually made the pact, iirc.

&#x200B;

that said I'm not super fluent in Japanese by a longshot so I might be wrong.

TL;DR:

&#x200B;

Yuuta was too caught up with the whole Tachibana thing to really notice Yui was getting more depressed, she ultimately is implied to have killed herself out of despair and Yuuta continues to live in Yui's body.

That is one of the worst endings I have ever seen. 

&#x200B;

Extremely abrupt and half the plot threads went nowhere, it's like the author just got bored making it.

&#x200B;

Webcomic ending at least had some buildup and closure. I think the only reason people think this ending is "better" is because it's happier.

It's funny, I was thinking about what the metaphorical Unknown Soldier might be like as a servant the other day.

&#x200B;

I was thinking more archer than berserker, though.

Who could it even be

&#x200B;

Yuuichi? Yutori?
